# Newtonite Ops — Engineering Rules

## Authorization
- Never rely on UI-only permissions; enforce team-scoped RBAC on the server for every query and mutation.

## Mutations on work items
- Every mutation on a work item MUST run inside a single `prisma.$transaction` that:
  1. Updates the work item (with version check for optimistic concurrency),
  2. Writes an append-only `ActivityEvent`,
  3. Enqueues an `OutboxJob` when needed (e.g. notifications, async side effects).

## Optimistic concurrency
- Use the `version` integer column on `WorkItem`.
- On version mismatch, return HTTP 409 Conflict with the latest work item state in the response body.

## Workflow and permissions
- Keep workflow rules and role-permission matrices in a single, clean module: `backend/src/services/workflowAndPermissions.ts`.
- This module should be easy to explain and modify live during demos or reviews.
